<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32488" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏlĭsīpo</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏlysippo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ulys-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Lusitania</i>, the modern
				<i>Lisbon</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 22,
				35, § 116</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 42, 67, §
			166</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Olysippo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 1, 19</span></i>
			: Ulysippo, Mela, 3, 1, 6.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏlĭsīpōnensis</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Olys-</span></b> ),
				e, adj., <i>of</i> or
				<i>belonging to Olisipo</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">promontorium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 21, 35, § 113</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏlĭsīpōnenses</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Olisipo</i>, <i>the
				Olisiponians</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 5, 4, §
		9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
